{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01745T9GUz5Ppn9Ri2d9JZZH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage main\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"bufio\"\n8\t\t\"fmt\"\n9\t\t\"math\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"strconv\"\n12\t\t\"strings\"\n13\t\n14\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n15\t)\n16\t\n17\tconst helpText = `Usage: seq [OPTION]... LAST\n18\t  or:  seq [OPTION]... FIRST LAST\n19\t  or:  seq [OPTION]... FIRST INCREMENT LAST\n20\tPrint numbers from FIRST to LAST, in steps of INCREMENT.\n21\t\n22\tMandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.\n23\t  -f, --format=FORMAT      use printf style floating-point FORMAT\n24\t  -s, --separator=STRING   use STRING to separate numbers (default: \\n)\n25\t  -w, --equal-width        equalize width by padding with leading zeroes\n26\t      --help        display this help and exit\n27\t      --version     output version information and exit\n28\t`\n29\t\n30\tconst versionText = `seq (go-unix-utils) dev\n31\t`\n32\t\n33\ttype options struct {\n34\t\tformat     string\n35\t\tseparator  string\n36\t\tequalWidth bool\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\tfunc main() {\n40\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n41\t\topts, operands, err := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n42\t\tif err != nil {\n43\t\t\texitWithError(err.Error())\n44\t\t}\n45\t\tfirst, incr, last, err := parseOperands(operands)\n46\t\tif err != nil {\n47\t\t\texitWithError(err.Error())\n48\t\t}\n49\t\tif incr == 0 {\n50\t\t\tstepStr := \"0\"\n51\t\t\tif len(operands) == 3 {\n52\t\t\t\tstepStr = operands[1]\n53\t\t\t}\n54\t\t\texitWithError(fmt.Sprintf(\"invalid Zero increment value: '%s'\", stepStr))\n55\t\t}\n56\t\tif opts.format != \"\" {\n57\t\t\tif opts.equalWidth {\n58\t\t\t\texitWithError(\"format string may not be specified when printing equal width strings\")\n59\t\t\t}\n60\t\t\tif err := validateFormat(opts.format); err != 